10 classes down. C, H and M to go. You can see I've saved
the harder classes for last. Buck was my second shot at a
tourist and I intended him to go for a hat trick but an
unfortunate incident with a !oPoly and his starting darts
ruined that. That was the only item polyed during the game,
polypiling is just too much work.

Buck the Rambler St:11 Dx:11 Co:16 In:13 Wi:10 Ch:14 Neutral
Dlvl:1  $:264 HP:10(10) Pw:2(2) AC:10 Exp:1 T:1

Buck was kind of good looking compared to most of my
characters and it made price IDing easier. And he was
healthy, otherwise Buck was ill suited to the task at hand.
It didn't help that the only BoH in the game was on the
penultimate level he explored in Gehennom.

Jumping boots were found on DL2, that was a big help early
on. The entrance to the mines was on DL4 so Buck popped in
to see if it was lit, alas it was dark and there was a big,
mean dwarf right by the stairs! Buck went back to the main
dungeon to look for Sokoban.

On DL 5 Samwise finally grew to a dog at 2421 turns.  This
was also the site of the aforementioned accident with the
!oPoly. Buck didn't even get anything useful for his darts,
19 +2 arrows! Nothing to be done but switch to daggers.

On DL8 Buck got some elven mithril! With most characters I
don't worry about spells until I get dragon scales and then
begin to convert to magic friendly garb. DL10 contained the
entrance to Sokoban.

Sokoban included some of the hairiest moments in the game.
First there was a swarm of killer bees and Buck had no
poison resistance and no unihorn. The camera and his
/oLightning he had just found got him by that one. Then on
the next level a green elf read a c?oCreateMonster. This
time Bucks first appeal to the Lady was heard at 4/55 HP.
The Treasure Zoo was challenging but not as dangerous since
Buck had the chance to prepare. In the end, Sokoban had
yielded an "oR, cold and sleep resistance, +2 e-mithril and
assorted food, wands and rings!

Back to the mines now, On ML6 there was a =oTC, a blindfold
(finally) and a magic whistle. ML7 was Mine Town, no great
boon there. Never could find the luckstone on the bottom but
got a luckstone from a gnome one level up! Strange. ML11 had
a poly trap so with his two pets and the magic whistle he
got a dragon and a gargoyle. The dragon killed two of the
shopkeepers (not Izchak) and later the cross aligned priest
when I was ready to convert the altar. I think this snapshot
was taken after finishing Sokoban and the mines.

Buck the Peregrinator    St:17 Dx:13 Co:18 In:13 Wi:10
Ch:14  
Dlvl:6  $:1968 HP:94(105) Pw:40(40) AC:-4 Xp:10/6747 T:12426 

Next excitement was Ludious. Buck killed almost all the
soldiers one at a time standing a knight's move from the
first door. Buck finally went after the dragons. He got in
pretty serious trouble a time or two, much jumping and
dodging was necessary a couple of times. Ultimately he got
orange scales. He went through both his /oUT on the gray to
no avail.

A temple to Blind Io was on DL13, eventually all the Ludious
gold was donated twice for 11 protection, Bartholomew the
gray dragon killed both priests, an Aleax donated a +3 long
sword and the Lady came through with Vorpral Blade,
Magicbane and much later, Mjollnir.

By the time Buck reached Medusa he still had no item to
cross water, well maybe he could have gone back for his
jumping boots, he still had no BoH and when he found speed
boots he went with those. Many stashes were made! He did
have =oPoly, =oPC and an "oUnchanging, so after killing all
the water monsters with rocks, he polyed into a Vampire Lord
and flew over to meet Medusa. Unfortunately he lost 2 XLs
when he polyed back.

DL27 had a throne room with 2 gray dragons and a black. The
black disintegrated Buck's gray dragon and his jabberwock,
sigh. Buck saved the two grays for last and carefully killed
them repeatedly so they both could be revived with one shot
from the /oUT. 22 Gray dragons later Buck had his gray
scales. Then he made a strange decision. He had Magicbane
and soon would have the PYEC. I would be sorta tourist like
to wear orange scale mail, a jaunty elven hat and a purple
and green hawaiian shirt! So he did!

A master lich met Buck when he went down to the castle level
and summoned nasties three times before Buck got things
under control. Buck was standing on the upstairs with a
couple of Elbereths engraved there but the ML was a knight's
move away and wouldn't come attack for a long time.

Finally buck qualified for the quest. The Master of Thieves
was no problem. Buck threw a !oPar at him and then stepped
up and lopped off his head on the first try! Boy, there's a
lot of stuff on the tourist quest. Very nice for a wishless,
polypileless game.

The next problem was in Juiblex's swamp. For reasons I can't
recall, Buck tamed some gremlins, it was night and he didn't
want to lose an intrinsic I guess. Well soon he had dozens
of 1 hp pet gremlins. He was surrounded and had no idea
where the land ended and the water started. Luckily, by now
he had some [BoLev and was able to displace gremlins an look
down until he found the stairs. He had a vague plan
involving leading the group upstair, locking himself in a
safe place and putting on his =oConflict but by the time he
got back they were all peaceful or feral and at the time
Buck had a pet titan who took care of the situation for him.

After some stash consolidation, more sacrificing and
enchanting stuff, Buck level teleported to the bottom to
find the VS. Buck worked his way up, casting light at every
upstairs and detect treasure on every level. An accident
with Mojo destroyed Orcus' wand. Buck had only one /oDeath
the whole game but never used but 3 charges.

He had 9 ?oMMap that he started using as soon as he thought
he was in the range where Vlad's might be. He found Vlad's
with his last scroll. Vlad, of course, was no contest. By
now Buck was stressed so he level teleported back to the
castle to sort his stuff again.

Back down this time collecting, digging paths, etc. The BoH
was found just before he ran out of levels to explore. 

Back to the castle, 42 db!oFH were mixed up, Buck drank
enough to get up to 250 HP. 40 holy water and 15 unholy
water were prepared. The first magic marker was used as
everything was foo proofed and enchanted. The armor didn't
need much work, Buck had a -39 AC when he first entered
Gehennom and only got -43 for the planes.

Buck level teleported to the portal to the wizard's tower,
walked up through the previously cleared tower to confront
Rodney. The first two shots from the /oDeath missed and Buck
decided to conserve his charges and just beat Rodney to
death. With a +6 Magicbane, +6 Long sword, +5 =oIncDam and
18/98 str, Rodney went down pretty fast.

Another level teleport to the bottom and then the ritual to
enter the sanctum. A /oSDD found the door to the temple and
quickly the Amulet was Buck's. The trip out proved to be
easier than expected. Only 4 !oGL had been found in the
entire game. These had been collected and cursed, but the
last time I made this trip I had 10.

43>44 40>42 39>40 35>36 35>35 was the extent of the
pullbacks, that would be 5 mysterious forces for a total of
ten levels.

Back in the castle, Buck couldn't part with all his pretty
potions so he made the trip to DL1 burdened. There he still
hated to throw them away so he quaffed until he was about
500 hp. Still burdened he put off the problem again, he
would take care of it on Astral.

Earth was easy, crystal ball and /oDig, Air was easy,
crystal ball and /oPoly for the air elementals, fire was
easy, crystal ball, then he even stopped to eat a giant to
get 18/** strength. Water was easy, oilskin cloak, continue
to levitate, crystal ball for starters and a /oSDD for final
course correction.

On Astral, he barely got his robe and his +5 =oIncDam back
on before he's beset by 2 master liches and an arch lich.
Burn Elbereth, drop the bag, name the liches so he can keep
up with which one he's working on at the moment. Once that
crisis was past, Buck decided he wanted to kill every
hostile priest, angel and adventurer on the Astral Plane!
I've never done that before. As it worked out the correct
altar was the last anyway and he was taking each opponent
down in just a few turns.

When he first met Famine he was about to go for his /oDeath
when he applied his stethoscope. Hmmm... killed him in one
turn. Later it took one or two, and Buck had plenty of food.

When he finally stood on the neutral altar with the Amulet,
he removed his =oFA and +5 +oIncDam to put on his two
=oAdornment. At charisma 25 he's sure to charm the crowd in
the demigod bar!

